Z||000000||Will||12-20-2001||03:51 PM||||There are too darn many screws in these fenders! Where are they all?<P>I've removed the ones in the wheel house, and I see the ones on teh top, though I haven't taken them out yet. Where are they at the rear edge and bottom corner?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Elenor84||12-20-2001||04:35 PM||||I just removed my 86SE Skirts...make sure u dont' miss the one's attatched the the fender and quarter panel.  Then there is quite a few up top there should be about 4 or 5 on the left side and about 3 on the right.  Now I suggest u wash it out so u can see all of them.  There are a couple that are hard to see because they are flat...u just need to poke something threw the center.  Most of mine are wrecked so I just used a dremel and drilled them out...I'm going to replace them with all new ones and with the screw type not the pulling ones...I suggest this for u as well...hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-20-2001||04:36 PM||||sorry was thinking of somethign else...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||12-20-2001||04:46 PM||||I removed the wheel wells, and the screws on top, but the fender still looks like it's secured by a couple of screws down where it attached to the side skirt.<P>DO I REALLY HAVE TO TAKE THE @#$%^& SIDE SKIRT OFF TO REMOVE THE FENDER?!?!?!?!?<BR>That's what it looks like. What a B!tch! What a PIMFA! Please tell me there's a simpler way.<BR>What stupid &^%$#@ at pontiac thought this one up?!?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||12-20-2001||04:57 PM||||Yep, you have to remove the rocker panels / skirts.  There are two rivets at the lower rear corner of each fender.<P>Don't forget the screws under the side marker.  I think there's also one at the upper front, partly obstructed by the hood.<BR>||||reg||1
